[al:新概念英语第一册]
[ti:143. A Walk Through the Woods]
[00:00.700]Lesson 143|第143课
[00:04.040]I live in a very old town,|我住在一个很古老的小镇上，
[00:07.910]which is surrounded by beautiful woods.|那里四周环绕着美丽的树林。
[00:11.310]It is a famous beauty spot.|它是一个著名的风景区。
[00:14.485]On Sundays, hundreds of people come from the city|每逢星期天，数以百计的人从城里来到我们的小镇，
[00:19.110]to see our town and to walk through the woods.|来参观我们的城镇，在树林中散步。
[00:23.795]Visitors have been asked to keep the woods clean and tidy.|游客们被要求保持树林整洁。
[00:29.69]Litter baskets have been placed under the trees.|树下放了废纸篓。
[00:34.045]But people still throw their rubbish everywhere.|但人们仍然随处乱扔垃圾。
[00:38.380]Last Wednesday,|上星期三，
[00:40.910]I went for a walk in the woods.|我到树林里散步。
[00:44.245]What I saw made me very sad.|我所见到的一切让我非常难过。
[00:48.970]I counted seven old cars and three old refrigerators.|我数了数，有7辆旧汽车和3台旧冰箱。
[00:55.745]The litter baskets were empty.|废纸篓是空的。
[00:58.955]And the ground was covered with pieces of paper,|地上铺满了碎纸、
[01:02.775]cigarette ends, old tires,|烟头、旧轮胎、
[01:06.440]empty bottles and rusty tins.|空瓶子和生锈的罐头盒。
[01:10.445]Among the rubbish,|在这些垃圾中，
[01:13.125]I found a sign which said,|我发现了一块牌子，上面写着：
[01:16.695]“Anyone who leaves litter in these woods|“凡在此树林里乱扔垃圾者，
[01:21.120]will be prosecuted.”|将受到法律的制裁。”